<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jhalawad</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jhalawad was one of the historic regions, or prants, of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kathiawar">Kathiawar</a> in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gujarat">Gujarat</a>, western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, in the north-east of the peninsula near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/little-rann-of-kutch">Little Rann of Kutch</a>. It took its name from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jhala">Jhala Rajputs</a>, who ruled several of its <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/princely-state">princely states</a>, including Dhrangadhra, Limbdi and Wadhwan. Its dry plains were known for <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cotton">cotton</a>, and it now lies mostly in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/surendranagar-district">Surendranagar district</a>.</p></div>
